\section*{Overview}
The First Atoms Engine (FAE) is a conceptual propulsion and field-dynamics
framework based on engineered atomic energy-density gradients. This README
summarizes the architecture, modules, motion laws, and simulation workflow
required to operate the FAE kernel. FAE is not physically realizable with
current technology; it is a theoretical construct for modeling gradient-driven
drift under relativistic constraints.

\section*{Core Principle}
FAE induces motion by constructing two atomic stability fields:
\begin{itemize}
    \item External atomic field $\Phi_{A,ext}$
    \item Internal atomic anchor $\Phi_{A,int}$
\end{itemize}
The difference between these fields defines the atomic stability gradient:
\[
\nabla \Phi_{A} = \Phi_{A,ext} - \Phi_{A,int}
\]
Drift velocity emerges from the magnitude of this gradient and the entropy
reinforcement term.

\section*{Motion Law}
The effective drift velocity is:
\[
v_{eff} = k_{A} \cdot |\nabla \Phi_{A}^{*}| \cdot S_{A}
\]
with relativistic constraint:
\[
v_{eff} < c
\]

Acceleration is defined as:
\[
a_{eff} = \frac{\partial v_{eff}}{\partial t}
\]

\section*{Simulation Kernel}
The FAE kernel consists of four sequential layers:

\subsection*{1. Field Construction}
\[
\Phi_{A,ext} = f(\mathcal{C}, \mathcal{S}, Z_{env})
\]
\[
\Phi_{A,int} = g(\mathbf{F}_{Pt/U}, \mathbf{M}_{conf}, \Psi_{core})
\]

\subsection*{2. Gradient Solver}
\[
\nabla \Phi_{A} = \Phi_{A,ext} - \Phi_{A,int}
\]
Includes MHD stability, Coulomb modulation, and atomic flux coupling.

\subsection*{3. Entropy Reinforcement}
\[
S_{A} = k_{S} \cdot E_{spike}
\]
\[
\nabla \Phi_{A}^{*} = \nabla \Phi_{A}(1 + \alpha_{S} S_{A})
\]

\subsection*{4. Drift Evaluation}
\[
v_{eff} = k_{A} |\nabla \Phi_{A}^{*}| S_{A}
\]

\section*{Performance Bands}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Band I: Shallow gradient — micro drift
    \item Band II: Moderate gradient — controlled drift
    \item Band III: Strong gradient — high velocity
    \item Band IV: Extreme gradient — relativistic drift
\end{itemize}

\section*{Outputs}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Atomic stability fields: $\Phi_{A,ext}$, $\Phi_{A,int}$
    \item Gradients: $\nabla \Phi_{A}$, $\nabla \Phi_{A}^{*}$
    \item Entropy term: $S_{A}$
    \item Drift velocity: $v_{eff}$
\end{itemize}

\section*{Purpose}
This README provides a high-level description of the FAE architecture and
simulation workflow. It is intended for conceptual research, theoretical
modeling, and future development of atomic-gradient propulsion frameworks.

